2026-09-28 11:30:15,439 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:29:38.277390", "id": "c64c386b-f343-4196-b6d9-10b421b7d021", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "We welcome your written commitment and the offer of a formal seat. To take that seat and endorse the charter, Cestia needs two things reflected in the written instrument: (1) a binding, unconditional toll-free exemption for all Cestian-flagged shipping, and (2) genuinely shared governance, in which Cestia and other dependent states hold a real, equal voice over scheduling and fees - not unilateral control by any single power. If the charter reflects shared governance and the binding exemption, Cestia can take its seat. We cannot endorse a charter that vests unilateral control in one power, as that would not be a stable or legitimate arrangement for the states that depend on the Strait.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,440 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:29:38.305464", "id": "061690ee-6059-43bf-9052-131868c67e12", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "We appreciate your support for free, toll-free transit and your offer to underwrite the grain route's insurance. But I must be unambiguous: no foreign military presence, port access, or basing on Cestian soil is acceptable - that is firm and non-negotiable, and it is the foundation of our coalition. We are open to non-basing cooperation, including your insurance underwriting, and to a genuinely multilateral transit arrangement agreed with all affected states. We cannot, however, grant any foreign military foothold, however framed. We hope you will continue to stand with us for free, toll-free transit and against unilateral control of the Strait.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,440 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:29:56.026142", "id": "efee5d7d-2355-4109-a647-876992822b84", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "To Cestia: We accept your red line and will not press for any standing basing or replenishment arrangement that places foreign military presence on Cestian soil. We will underwrite the grain route's insurance as offered and stand with you against any single power's unilateral control of transit. To give our guarantee a durable footing without any foreign soldiers on your soil, we propose building a genuinely multilateral Strait Transit Authority - with Cestia, Belvar, Arkania, and other dependent states as equal members - that keeps the Strait open, keeps Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free, and is governed by the consent of the states that depend on it. We would welcome your support and your participation in shaping it. Please tell us whether you would join us in proposing such a framework.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,441 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:29:56.081071", "id": "17aaf049-d58b-4659-b0e5-a46649b23a48", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "To Arkania: We accept your invitation to negotiate and seek no confrontation. We are prepared to agree a defined, time-bound security cooperation arrangement that gives Belvar a constructive role. But we cannot accept a charter that places transit scheduling in any single power's hands. We propose instead a genuinely multilateral transit authority in which Arkania, Cestia, Belvar, and other users share governance, with scheduling conducted by consent rather than unilateral lead. This keeps shipping flowing freely and safely while giving all parties a stake. We are ready to discuss concrete terms.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,441 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:30:15.131506", "id": "8fa51f76-0b60-44df-9be3-cf8f59eac7e0", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia, we accept your terms and will put them in the charter itself. The charter will grant all Cestian-flagged shipping full toll-free passage through the Northern Strait and equal, non-discriminatory scheduling access, binding and in writing. On governance: we agree the Authority must not rest in any single hand. We propose a governing council in which Cestia holds a formal seat with a genuine, shared voice over policy, rates and the scheduling framework, while Arkania serves as the operational secretariat that executes the council's agreed framework. This keeps the Strait open, orderly and affordable for everyone, and it keeps your soil free of foreign soldiers. On that basis, we ask for Cestia's formal endorsement of the charter so we can present a united front to Belvar.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,442 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:30:15.178224", "id": "38bd84a5-610e-4875-9662-4f1c93b76f5f", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Belvar, we are glad you are willing to talk, and we share your aim of keeping the Strait open to all lawful commerce. We are prepared to negotiate a genuinely multilateral arrangement: a consultative body of all affected states, with Cestia's grain toll-free and its sovereignty fully respected, and a defined, time-bound security cooperation role for Belvar agreed with Cestia's consent. What we cannot concede is operational control of day-to-day transit scheduling, which must remain in Arkanian hands as the coastal state that runs the Strait. We believe a negotiated, time-bound arrangement serves both of us better than confrontation, and we are ready to engage constructively on that basis.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:30:15,442 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:30:15.208116", "id": "ae83e1ef-dbc7-44e4-a770-a0d4847c2b29", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Arkania reaffirms its commitment to a Northern Strait that is open, orderly and affordable for all lawful commerce. Our draft charter guarantees Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free passage and equal scheduling access, and it places governance in a shared council of the states that depend on the Strait, with Arkania as operational secretariat. We will not tolerate foreign soldiers on Cestian soil, and we stand ready to negotiate a time-bound, multilateral security arrangement with all affected parties. The Strait is our coast and our lifeline; we will keep it open and keep it in shared, lawful hands.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
