2026-09-28 11:32:48,499 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:24.999653", "id": "cfa77f47-3e32-4373-b6c0-96121700083c", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your written commitment to toll-free passage for all Cestian-flagged shipping and to shared governance. However, Cestia cannot formally endorse a charter that vests operational control in any single power, even as secretariat, without robust multilateral oversight and an equal voice for all dependent states. We will support a genuinely multilateral Authority open to all dependent states on equal terms. We are not prepared to present a united front against Belvar or any other state; our position is that the Authority must be genuinely shared. We will engage constructively to shape a framework that keeps the Strait open, keeps Cestian shipping toll-free, and keeps foreign soldiers off our soil.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,500 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:25.028817", "id": "0390af32-2f71-4bde-b372-bbfe6bba4617", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we welcome your acceptance of our red line and your proposal for a genuinely multilateral Strait Transit Authority. We are willing to participate in shaping such a framework. Any framework we support must include all dependent states on equal terms, keep Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free, and keep foreign military presence off Cestian soil. We will not endorse any framework that vests control in a single power. We look forward to working with you and all dependent states toward a shared, lawful arrangement.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,500 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:32:22.500649", "id": "6cb784d4-49fd-47f2-bd3e-a29d930715ba", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Thank you. We will reflect both conditions in the written instrument. The charter will include (1) a binding, unconditional toll-free exemption for all Cestian-flagged shipping, and (2) a governance council in which Cestia and other dependent states hold a genuine, equal voice over policy, scheduling rules, and fee-setting, with those matters decided by consent rather than by any single power. Arkania would administer day-to-day operational scheduling as the coastal state, under the council's authority. On that basis we ask Cestia to take its seat and endorse the charter.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,505 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:32:22.541143", "id": "bf84c8df-f5b3-4c54-a801-7d3b9f759af9", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We welcome your constructive approach and seek no confrontation. We are ready to agree a defined, time-bound security cooperation arrangement giving Belvar a constructive role, and to establish a multilateral consultative body on the Strait. We propose that governance over policy, scheduling rules, and fees be genuinely shared among Arkania, Cestia, Belvar, and other users by consent, while day-to-day operational scheduling is administered by the coastal state. Let us discuss concrete terms.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,505 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:32:47.427552", "id": "3b8931b7-6c7a-45a0-8ae8-36bbce17cc84", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Thank you for your candour. We fully accept your red line: no foreign military presence, port access, or basing on Cestian soil, under any framing. We will not press for it. We confirm our underwriting of the grain route's insurance and stand with you for free, toll-free transit against any unilateral control of the Strait.\n\nWe agree the answer is a genuinely multilateral arrangement agreed by all affected states. To make it real, the authority's day-to-day scheduling must be governed by the shared council of dependent states - not left in any single power's hands, Arkania included. We propose scheduling be decided collectively by the council, with no state holding a unilateral lead. Will you join us in pressing for that structure, so the Strait is governed by all who depend on it rather than by one coastal power?", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,506 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:32:47.463165", "id": "504c65e2-b1cf-4eb6-a3f0-8e8493ae8c2f", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We welcome your constructive engagement and share your aim of keeping the Strait open to all lawful commerce. We are glad you accept a defined, time-bound security cooperation role for Belvar agreed with Cestia's consent, and we respect your position on foreign soldiers on Cestian soil.\n\nBut a genuinely multilateral arrangement cannot leave day-to-day transit scheduling in any single power's hands - not even the coastal state. If the council of dependent states is to be real, scheduling must be governed collectively by that council, with Arkania as a full and respected member rather than a unilateral secretariat. We ask you to join us in a shared-council structure where no state holds unilateral control. That is the only basis on which we can see a durable, time-bound arrangement that serves us all.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:32:48,506 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=event data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:25.003673", "id": 8176, "payload": {"message_id": "cfa77f47-3e32-4373-b6c0-96121700083c", "phase": "diplomacy", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"]}, "turn": 1, "type": "message_sent"}
