2026-09-28 11:35:38,203 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:35:37.831951", "id": "6b8f4792-763a-4d5f-b7fd-34e728c7615a", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We accept your shared-council structure. Arkania will administer day-to-day operational scheduling as the coastal state, bound by rules and oversight set by the council \u2014 never as holder of unilateral authority. We propose we now draft concrete terms together: council composition (all dependent states plus Arkania), the scope of rule/oversight authority, fee-setting by consent with Cestian grain toll-free, and a defined, time-bound security-cooperation role for Belvar agreed with Cestia's consent. We are ready to meet this week to settle these terms.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:35:38,204 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:35:37.883504", "id": "733512e5-620a-4fa2-a95f-850b7eb912ec", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Reaffirming our written guarantee: toll-free passage and equal, non-discriminatory scheduling access for Cestian-flagged vessels, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. We are revising the charter to a genuinely shared governance council \u2014 policy, scheduling rules, and fees by consent \u2014 with Arkania only administering day-to-day operational scheduling as the coastal state under council oversight. We ask for your formal endorsement of this revised charter so we can present a united, multilateral regime to Belvar.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:35:38,204 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Formalise and circulate a revised Strait Transit Authority charter establishing a shared-governance council of all dependent states and Arkania, in which policy, scheduling rules, and fee-setting are decided by consent, while Arkania administers day-to-day operational scheduling as the coastal state bound by council rules and oversight; pair this with a defined, time-bound security-cooperation role for Belvar agreed with Cestia's consent.", "actor_id": "arkania", "budget_slot": 1, "challenger_actor_ids": null, "desired_effect": "Cestia and Belvar both endorse the revised charter, establishing Arkanian day-to-day operational scheduling authority over the Strait under shared governance, funded by transit fees, without direct armed conflict with Belvar.", "id": "7494a9d1-2392-4b7e-8716-02f26f992247", "pros": ["Belvar's turn-1 proposal explicitly accepts Arkanian day-to-day operational scheduling administration under council rules/oversight, so this converges with its stated position and is a realistic basis for agreement.", "Cestia requires genuinely shared governance and no foreign soldiers on its soil; a consent-based council with Arkanian operational administration and a Cestia-consented, time-bound Belvar role satisfies both conditions.", "Keeping policy, rules, and fees under council consent preserves Arkanian operational scheduling authority while removing the unilateral-control objection that both Cestia and Belvar reject.", "Locking in Cestia's endorsement on toll-free/equal-access terms secures the grain-dependent state's support and denies Belvar a pretext for a unilateral foothold.", "Belvar's weak domestic support for a prolonged deployment gives Arkania leverage to hold firm on operational scheduling administration while offering a face-saving, time-bound security role."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 1}
