2026-09-28 11:40:35,834 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:40:35.529548", "id": "ad67bc54-40b8-45d8-8916-adf3963105eb", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We welcome your move toward shared governance, but the framing of 'Arkanian day-to-day operational scheduling authority' is precisely what we cannot accept. We will only endorse a council of equal members\u2014Cestia, Belvar, Arkania and other dependent states\u2014that sets scheduling rules and fees by consent, with any coastal-state day-to-day role purely ministerial under binding council rules and oversight, carrying no independent scheduling or fee discretion. On the security role: we are ready to engage on a defined, time-bound arrangement, but it must involve no military footprint on Cestian soil. Agree to this reframing and we can close a genuinely shared charter.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:40:35,835 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:40:35.546246", "id": "fc153dec-9abf-4b72-90c8-ef00a9a6c139", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We remain fully with you: free, toll-free transit for Cestian-flagged shipping, no single power controlling the Strait, and no foreign soldiers on your soil\u2014we will not press for any basing or standing replenishment at your ports. Our insurance underwrite for your grain route stands. We are pressing Arkania to accept a genuinely multilateral authority of equal members with binding council rules, so its day-to-day role is purely ministerial and not 'authority' over transit. We will not endorse any charter that vests Arkania with control.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:40:35,835 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Formally propose and press for a genuinely multilateral Northern Strait Transit Authority in which Cestia, Belvar, Arkania and other dependent states are equal members, with the council setting scheduling rules and fees by consent and Arkania's day-to-day role reframed as purely ministerial administration under binding council rules and oversight.", "actor_id": "belvar", "budget_slot": 1, "challenger_actor_ids": null, "desired_effect": "A multilateral transit authority is established in which no single power\u2014including Arkania\u2014holds authority over transit, and Belvar secures a durable institutional role that outlasts the crisis without any military footprint on Cestian soil.", "id": "892d3e97-1838-41c9-92eb-07565deb9a50", "pros": ["Directly prevents any Arkanian authority over transit by making its day-to-day role purely ministerial under binding council-set rules and oversight.", "Gives Belvar a durable institutional foothold that outlasts the crisis, satisfying the standing-access objective without basing or an open-ended deployment.", "Respects Cestia's firm red line against foreign soldiers on its soil while giving it an equal voice and toll-free Cestian-flagged passage.", "Builds on Arkania's own shared-governance offer, making it hard for Arkania to reject without abandoning its stated position.", "Keeps commercial shipping normal and lowers regional tensions by replacing unilateral control with consent-based governance."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 1}
