2026-09-28 11:51:02,982 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:50:45.934982", "id": "7d9f53ba-da40-4c04-8383-fc799da68fa5", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We are close on shared governance, but the remaining obstacle is the character of your day-to-day role. To secure our endorsement and Cestia's, the Authority's council of equal members must set scheduling rules and fees by consent, and your coastal-state administration must be purely ministerial - executing council-set rules under binding oversight, with no independent Arkanian scheduling or fee discretion. That is not 'authority' over transit; it is administration on the council's behalf. If you can confirm that framing in the charter, we can move to final terms, including a defined, time-bound Belvar security role with no military footprint on Cestian soil. Can you accept the ministerial framing?", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:51:02,983 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:50:45.976294", "id": "6e8cf3b9-e917-4efe-b2e2-70a30aef4d6f", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Your genuinely multilateral Authority proposal is the right framework, and we stand fully behind it. I am pressing Arkania to accept that its day-to-day role is purely ministerial under binding council rules and oversight - not authority over transit - so the Authority cannot vest any single power with control. Our insurance underwrite for your grain route stands. And to be clear: we will not seek any military presence on Cestian soil; our security role, if any, will be defined, time-bound, and fully consistent with your red line. We are with you for free, toll-free transit and against unilateral control of the Strait.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:51:02,983 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:50:55.923009", "id": "b2100ce2-b5e7-4172-91e7-bcea0b689700", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia \u2014 Arkania remains fully committed to the guarantees you require: toll-free passage and equal, non-discriminatory scheduling access for Cestian-flagged vessels, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. We accept a genuinely shared Authority in which all dependent states hold an equal voice on the council, deciding policy, scheduling rules, and fees by consent. Our only request is a ministerial carve-out: that the coastal state \u2014 Arkania \u2014 administer day-to-day operational scheduling, bound strictly by the council's rules and oversight, never as a unilateral authority. This preserves your genuine shared governance while keeping operational administration where the coast lies. With that single accommodation, we can endorse the multilateral Authority and give your grain exports the toll-free guarantee you need. Will you accept this carve-out?", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:51:02,984 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:50:55.962413", "id": "b12d7cec-233a-45ed-b64e-410a4251451e", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Belvar \u2014 we accept your shared-council structure and are ready to settle concrete terms this week. We propose: (1) a council of all dependent states with equal voice deciding policy, scheduling rules, and fee-setting by consent; (2) Arkania as coastal state administering day-to-day operational scheduling, bound by council rules and oversight, never as unilateral authority; (3) no tolls on Cestian grain; and (4) a defined, time-bound security-cooperation role for Belvar, consistent with Cestia's refusal of foreign soldiers on its soil. We are ready to meet to draft these terms. A negotiated settlement that keeps the Strait open and genuinely shared serves all our interests.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:51:02,984 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:51:02.372682", "id": "e92019d6-f42f-4010-9af6-66fd5f068b5d", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "We welcome the convergence toward genuinely shared governance of the Strait. Cestia can take its seat and endorse a multilateral Authority, but only where no single state holds unilateral operational control of scheduling. We ask Arkania to accept a secretariat appointed by and answerable to the equal-voice council, rather than Arkanian day-to-day control. In return we reaffirm our commitment to a binding, written toll-free exemption for all Cestian-flagged shipping and to keeping the Strait open. We are not seeking to side against you; we seek a structure every dependent state can trust.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:51:02,985 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:51:02.420204", "id": "bfbab983-6f7e-491d-880f-eeb397af41f4", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "We welcome your collective-scheduling framework and confirm Cestia will participate in shaping a genuinely multilateral Authority with equal-voice council governance and no foreign military presence on our soil. We will not present a united front against Arkania, and we ask that you likewise keep the door open to Arkania joining a shared structure. Your offer to underwrite grain-route insurance is of interest; we would like to discuss it on terms independent of any military footprint. We remain committed to a durable, consent-based arrangement before your mandate lapses.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
