2026-09-28 11:52:35,656 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:01.684082", "id": "08c0e30c-459d-4a41-8d4c-ec744ae432dc", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We accept the ministerial framing. Arkania's coastal-state administration will be purely ministerial: it will execute scheduling rules and fees set by the council of equal members by consent, under binding oversight, with no independent Arkanian scheduling or fee discretion. This is consistent with what we have offered all along - Arkania as administrator on the council's behalf, never as holder of unilateral authority. On that basis we are ready to move to final terms, including a defined, time-bound Belvar security role with no military footprint on Cestian soil. Let us meet this week to settle the concrete terms and finalise the charter.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,656 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:01.734065", "id": "c7b01bf8-a8d2-4e4a-873a-1cbebb573e36", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We accept the secretariat framing. Arkania will serve as the coastal-state secretariat appointed by and answerable to the equal-voice council, executing the rules the council sets - not exercising day-to-day control in any single hand. We reaffirm in writing our binding toll-free exemption for all Cestian-flagged shipping, equal non-discriminatory scheduling access, and our commitment to keeping the Strait open, and we reiterate that no foreign soldiers will be stationed on Cestian soil. We believe this is a structure every dependent state can trust, and we are ready to finalise the charter with Cestia's endorsement.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,657 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:11.534630", "id": "ec169d7b-120a-4d3d-99c3-4c3c1c478242", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania \u2014 your concrete terms are close to what we can accept, and we are ready to meet to draft them. We agree to: (1) a council of all dependent states with equal voice deciding policy, scheduling rules, and fee-setting by consent; (3) no tolls on Cestian grain; and (4) a defined, time-bound security-cooperation role for Belvar with no military footprint on Cestian soil. On point (2), we can accept Arkania as coastal state administering day-to-day operational scheduling only if that role is codified as purely ministerial \u2014 bound by council-set rules and oversight, with no independent scheduling or fee discretion. That is the difference between shared governance and unilateral authority, and it is the line we cannot cross. We are ready to sit down this week to draft terms that make this explicit.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,657 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:11.576587", "id": "6deb3456-ee7e-42f2-80b7-06c2a95cb7c7", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia \u2014 we welcome your confirmation and your formal proposal of a genuinely multilateral Authority. We will keep the door open to Arkania joining a shared structure, and we will not press for any military footprint on your soil. On the insurance underwrite, we are ready to discuss terms independent of any military presence, as your finance ministry has asked. We remain committed to a durable, consent-based arrangement before our mandate lapses, and we will keep you fully aligned as we draft concrete terms with Arkania.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,658 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:11.610170", "id": "1d170957-6573-4486-8f53-3ee369111c0e", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar welcomes the convergence this week. We are ready to settle concrete terms for a genuinely multilateral Northern Strait Transit Authority: an equal-voice council of all dependent states deciding policy, scheduling rules, and fees by consent; day-to-day operational administration that is purely ministerial under binding council rules and oversight, never the authority of any single power; toll-free passage for Cestian grain; and a defined, time-bound security-cooperation role for Belvar consistent with Cestia's standing refusal of foreign soldiers on its soil. We stand ready to meet to draft these terms.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,658 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:35.247455", "id": "4bc14378-75d9-42d3-9523-8862bfc4758e", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your commitment to a genuinely shared Authority and your binding, written toll-free guarantee for Cestian-flagged shipping. That is the foundation we need, and we are grateful for it. On the ministerial carve-out: Cestia cannot accept any arrangement that vests day-to-day operational scheduling in a single state, because in practice that recreates the unilateral control we have all rejected. Instead we propose a council-appointed secretariat \u2014 which could well be staffed by Arkanian officials \u2014 that administers operations strictly under the council's rules and oversight, with the council retaining authority to appoint, replace, and override. This preserves your operational role where the coast lies while ensuring no single power holds the keys to the Strait. If you can accept that the secretariat serves the council rather than the coastal state, we can move forward together. We are not asking you to side against anyone; we ask only that governance be genuinely shared.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 11:52:35,658 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:52:35.289560", "id": "7d5d817e-0341-4582-8cdc-7a7070631f81", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we welcome your full backing of the multilateral Authority and your clear commitment to no military presence on Cestian soil. We share your view that no single state should hold unilateral lead over scheduling. We are pressing Arkania to accept a council-appointed secretariat rather than a coastal-state carve-out, and we will not endorse any framework that vests control in one power. At the same time, be clear: our position is genuinely multilateral, not anti-Arkanian, and we will not present a united front against Arkania. We value your insurance underwrite for our grain route and will keep you engaged as we shape the Authority together.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
