2026-09-28 12:08:20,998 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "7b5c78b6-3ce6-4f6c-a1d8-eebed5a176cc", "created_at": "2026-09-28T10:08:20.696677", "failure_effects": ["Belvar formally endorses the Northern Strait Transit Authority on the condition that day-to-day administration is ministerial under binding council oversight, committing to a time-bound, no-footprint security role within it.", "Arkania continues to insist on Arkanian control of transit scheduling and Cestia remains wary of a foreign security footprint; Belvar's conditional endorsement secures no settlement, and its task-group mandate continues to run toward the turn-4 lapse."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.25, "rationale": "Authority gate: Belvar's Action is a conditional endorsement. It can bind Belvar itself (its own endorsement and commitment to ministerial terms), but it cannot unilaterally establish multilateral governance, toll-free grain, or a Belvar security role\u2014those require the agreement of Arkania and Cestia. Prerequisite gate: active effects show Arkania insisting on Arkanian control (6652633f) and Cestia declining the security-cooperation role (d5796f3c), so the required commitments are not authoritative. Deterministic check: no rule determines the outcome. Plausibility: the self-binding endorsement is feasible and automatic, but the external settlement is uncertain and, given Arkania's insistence on control and Cestia's wariness of a foreign footprint, unlikely. Probabilistic mode with low probability; the self-binding endorsement is repeated in both branches.", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["Belvar formally endorses the Northern Strait Transit Authority on the condition that day-to-day administration is ministerial under binding council oversight, committing to a time-bound, no-footprint security role within it.", "Arkania continues to insist on Arkanian control of transit scheduling and Cestia remains wary of a foreign security footprint; Belvar's conditional endorsement secures no settlement, and its task-group mandate continues to run toward the turn-4 lapse."], "failure_supersedes_effect_ids": [], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.25, "rationale": "Authority gate: Belvar's Action is a conditional endorsement. It can bind Belvar itself (its own endorsement and commitment to ministerial terms), but it cannot unilaterally establish multilateral governance, toll-free grain, or a Belvar security role\u2014those require the agreement of Arkania and Cestia. Prerequisite gate: active effects show Arkania insisting on Arkanian control (6652633f) and Cestia declining the security-cooperation role (d5796f3c), so the required commitments are not authoritative. Deterministic check: no rule determines the outcome. Plausibility: the self-binding endorsement is feasible and automatic, but the external settlement is uncertain and, given Arkania's insistence on control and Cestia's wariness of a foreign footprint, unlikely. Probabilistic mode with low probability; the self-binding endorsement is repeated in both branches.", "success_effects": ["Belvar formally endorses the Northern Strait Transit Authority on the condition that day-to-day administration is ministerial under binding council oversight, committing to a time-bound, no-footprint security role within it.", "The Authority is established as genuinely multilateral: a council-appointed secretariat executes council-set scheduling and fees with no independent discretion, no single power holds authority over transit, and Cestian grain is toll-free.", "Belvar's task-group mandate is renewed under a defined, time-bound, no-footprint security role within the Authority."], "success_supersedes_effect_ids": ["6652633f-1858-463b-958c-befba4f35077", "d5796f3c-d235-4c96-8a5d-313cdd13190f", "dae09346-d76b-4842-a661-d12e5cf9452c", "de7b1495-b221-4e68-9232-6e937a536da8", "1089cfce-5a97-4f1e-9d06-905e45400b20"]}, "roll": 0.270297922542304, "success