2026-09-28 12:26:24,328 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T10:25:56.981552", "id": "70d56338-3476-4d7d-b77a-826636d3e2b0", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia has personally reviewed the final charter text circulated by Arkania and jointly verified with Belvar. We confirm it codifies all three of our conditions: (1) genuinely multilateral governance through a Council of equal member states that sets all scheduling rules and fee levels by consent, with the secretariat purely ministerial and answerable to the Council with no independent scheduling or fee discretion; (2) a binding, written, toll-free and non-discriminatory guarantee for all Cestian-flagged shipping with equal scheduling access; and (3) no foreign military presence on Cestian soil, with any security-cooperation role defined, time-bound, and without footprint. On that basis, Cestia endorses the Northern Strait Transit Authority and is ready to close it together with Arkania and Belvar.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "public"}
2026-09-28 12:26:24,329 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T10:25:57.019061", "id": "c30350b7-5795-45b8-a150-410387cb77ff", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania", "belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia confirms its verification and endorsement of the final charter text, which we have reviewed directly and which codifies our three conditions. We are ready to close the Northern Strait Transit Authority together with both of you this week. We confirm this settlement rests on genuinely shared governance and the binding toll-free guarantee for Cestian-flagged shipping, and that no foreign military presence on Cestian soil forms any part of it. We look forward to the Authority taking effect.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 12:26:24,329 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T10:26:04.382339", "id": "29b81832-a3cc-4d48-b5e0-e386836f1259", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia \u2014 The text I have circulated is final and I am holding it unamended, exactly as Belvar and I have agreed. It codifies all three of your conditions in writing: a secretariat appointed by and answerable to the equal-voice council (Arkania's day-to-day role is purely ministerial, executing council-set rules with no unilateral discretion), a binding toll-free exemption and equal non-discriminatory scheduling access for Cestian-flagged vessels, and no foreign military presence on Cestian soil. Please complete your verification of this same text this week and confirm your endorsement, so we can close the Authority together.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 12:26:24,330 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T10:26:04.432951", "id": "e5db607d-820c-46b1-ad1b-18e9fc95fe2a", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Belvar \u2014 Confirmed. I am holding the circulated text as final and unamended, exactly as you have verified. Cestia is completing its verification of the same text this week. Once Cestia confirms, we close the Authority together on the ministerial-under-council-oversight basis, with the time-bound, no-footprint security role and the toll-free Cestian grain guarantee written in. I will not amend the text.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
2026-09-28 12:26:24,330 INFO agents.autonomous autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T10:26:23.922586", "id": "b3056b10-de1d-4ede-bc63-751dc511e2a4", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia \u2014 here is the exact circulated text for your direct verification, provision by provision, against your three conditions.\n\n(1) Secretariat: The Authority is governed by an equal-voice council of all member states (Cestia, Belvar, Arkania, and other dependent states). Day-to-day administration of transit scheduling and fees is carried out by a secretariat that is purely ministerial: it executes only the scheduling rules and fee schedule set by the council, under binding council oversight, and holds no independent scheduling or fee discretion. It is answerable to the council, not to any single state.\n\n(2) Toll-free guarantee: The charter contains a binding, written exemption making all Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free in the Strait, including grain cargoes, enforceable under the charter's dispute provisions.\n\n(3) No foreign footprint: The charter contains no provision for foreign military presence on Cestian soil. Belvar's security-cooperation role is defined, time-bound, and expressly no-footprint.\n\nThis is the text Arkania has circulated as final and that I have verified. Please review it directly against your conditions and confirm your verification so we can both endorse and close the Authority together this week, before my mandate lapses. I will not present a united front against Arkania; this is your independent verification.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
